From: alesx2io <96351978+alesx2io@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:20:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dash: overlay: dim the screen to the HyperOS level

config_screenBrightnessDimFloat was the panel minimum (2 nits), so the
dim phase before the screen timeout looked like the screen turned off.
This is easy to hit with apps that release FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON while in
use (MIUI Camera does after some idle time): the screen stays dimmed
until the timeout, while the brightness slider still shows the user value.

HyperOS dims to config_screenBrightnessDim_hyper (15 on the 0-255 scale);
use the same level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml
index 0189185..d1100d7 100644
--- a/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml
@@ -76,8 +76,11 @@
 
     <!-- Screen brightness used to dim the screen when the user activity
          timeout expires.  May be less than the minimum allowed brightness setting
-         that can be set by the user. -->
-    <item name="config_screenBrightnessDimFloat" format="float" type="dimen">0.000854597</item>
+         that can be set by the user.
+         HyperOS ignores this value and dims to config_screenBrightnessDim_hyper (15 on the
+         0-255 scale); use the same level instead of the panel minimum (2 nits), which made
+         the screen look off while dimmed, for example with the camera open. -->
+    <item name="config_screenBrightnessDimFloat" format="float" type="dimen">0.05511811</item>
 
     <!-- Array of light sensor lux values to define our levels for auto backlight brightness support.
          The N entries of this array define N + 1 control points as follows:
-- 
2.56.1

